  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The Fanuc post has a new option, `rigidTapM29` (\"Rigid tap M29 before G84\"). It is off by default.\n- When the option is on, the post writes `M29 S<rpm>` on the block right before each G84 block that opens a cycle group.\n- G80 ends rigid mode on the control. Thus each G84 group writes its own M29.\n- When the option is on and the section has no spindle speed (for example a touch probe section at 0 rpm), the post refuses the G84 by name. It does not write `M29 S0`.\n- This is the slice for question 1 of #2603 (M29 before G84). Question 2 (G73 or G83, the R plane) still waits for the machine owner.\n\n## Cause\n\nOn a 30i/31i/32i control, G84 is rigid without M29 only when parameter 5200 bit 0 is set. The post wrote no M29. A control without that setting needs `M29 S..` before G84. The owner has not said which setting his 31i-A5 has, so the post gets an option.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew file `crates/post/tests/fanuc_rigid_tap.rs`:\n\n- `fanuc_rigid_tap_m29_is_off_by_default`: no M29 when the option is not set.\n- `fanuc_rigid_tap_m29_precedes_each_g84_group`: three G84 groups, each with `M29 S600` on the block before it, and no M29 on the drill operation.\n- `fanuc_rigid_tap_m29_without_spindle_speed_is_refused_by_name`: a tap with no spindle speed is refused by name, with no M29 and no G84.\n- `fanuc_rigid_tap_m29_option_is_declared_off`: the option is declared with the default `false`.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- Unchanged post: `..._precedes_each_g84_group` and `..._option_is_declared_off` fail (red). The default test passes, as expected.\n- Speed guard disabled: `..._without_spindle_speed_is_refused_by_name` fails (red). Restored: all four pass.\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 120 steps, 0 failed. The steps are all the post suites and the app suites that read `fanuc.cps`, including `conformance`, `rigid_tapping` and `posting`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `fanuc_aicc` (7 tests) still passes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The option is off by default. Every golden stays byte-identical.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a real control. The owner's 31i-A5 graphic check is the next step when the option is on.\n- No heavy lanes run. The diff reaches no geometry or motion code.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3441 touches `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` in `declaredOptions` and in `onCycle` (one line, the `aiccOff()` call that is already on main). It does not change the G84 or G99 lines that this PR changes. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/2603-fanuc-m29.md`.\n\nChangelog: Fanuc post: a new option, \"Rigid tap M29 before G84\" (off by default), writes `M29 S<rpm>` before each G84 cycle group for a control that taps rigid only after M29.\n\nRefs #2603\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
